REGENT OF KEPAHIANG

BENGKULU PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF KEPAHIANG REGENCY NUMBER 10 OF 2016

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

AGAINST ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF KEPAHIANG,

Considering:
a. that every citizen has the right to survival, growth, and development, to obtain protection of personal self, honor and dignity as a complete human being in family, community, national and state life;
b. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence and discrimination;
c. that all forms of acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;
d. that violence against women and children in Kepahiang Regency continues to increase both quantitatively and qualitatively, so that prevention, protection, recovery and law enforcement efforts are needed;
e. that legislation regarding the protection of women and children victims of violence requires the support of regulations and institutional arrangements at the Kepahiang Regency level that can guarantee its implementation;
f. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, letter d and letter e, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of Kepahiang concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of:
1. Article 18 Paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Againts Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
3. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 138 concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
5. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 182 concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);
6. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
7. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);
8. Law Number 39 of 2003 concerning the Establishment of Lebong and Kepahiang Regencies in Bengkulu Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 154, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4349);
9. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
10. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
11. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
12. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);
13. Law Number 6 of 2014 Concerning Villages (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 7, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5495);
14. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
15. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4644);
16. Government Regulation Number 39 of 2012 Concerning the Implementation of Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Nomr 68, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5294);
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 56);
18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 Concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Integrated Service Centers.

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF KEPAHIANG REGENCY and

CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The principles of protection of children and women who are victims of violence are:

a. respect and fulfillment of victims' rights as human rights;
b. justice and equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. rights-based handling; and
e. best interests of the victim.

text:
Pasal 3

Tujuan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak adalah:
a. mencegah tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak; b. menghapus segala bentuk kekerasan dan eksploitasi terhadap perempuan dan anak;
c. melindungi, dan memberikan rasa aman bagi perempuan dan anak; d. memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak baik sebagai korban tindak kekerasan, maupun sebagai pelapor,dan saksi;
e. menjamin penanganan dan penyelesaian tindak kekerasan terhadap  perempuan dan anak secara adil dan bermartabat; danf. melakukan pemulihan dan pemberdayaan kepada perempuan dan anak  korban tindak kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 3

The objectives of protection of women and children are:

a. to prevent acts of violence against women and children;
b. to eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. to protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. to provide services to women and children both as victims of acts of violence, as well as reporters and witnesses;
e. to guarantee the handling and resolution of acts of violence against women and children in a fair and dignified manner; and
f. to carry out recovery and empowerment of women and child victims of acts of violence.

text:
BAB II

HAK–HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK KORBAN KEKERASAN

Pasal 5

Setiap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan mempunyai hak sebagai  berikut:
a. hak untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia; b. hak atas pemulihan kesehatan dan psikologis dari penderitaan yang  dialami korban;
c. hak menentukan sendiri keputusannya;
d. hak mendapatkan informasi;
e. hak atas kerahasiaan identitasnya;
f. hak atas penanganan pengaduan;
g. hak atas pendampingan dan bantuan hukum;
h. hak untuk mendapatkan kemudahan dalam proses peradilan; dan i. hak atas kompensasi;
j. hak atas pemulihan sosial;

translated_text:
CHAPTER II

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILD VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 5

Every woman and child victim of violence has the following rights:

a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings;
b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality of identity;
f. the right to complaint handling;
g. the right to assistance and legal aid;
h. the right to obtain facilities in the judicial process; and
i. the right to compensation;
j. the right to social recovery;

text:
Pasal 6

Anak korban kekerasan selain mendapatkan hak-hak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5, juga mendapatkan hak-hak khusus, sebagai  berikut:
a. hak penghormatan atas kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang; b. hak pelayanan dasar;
c. hak perlindungan yang sama;
d. hak bebas dari berbagai stigma; dane. hak mendapatkan kebebasan.

translated_text:
Article 6

Child victims of violence in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 5, also obtain special rights, as follows:

a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and
e. the right to obtain freedom.

text:
BAB III

TINDAK KEKERASAN TERHADAP PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK

Pasal 7

Bentuk-bentuk kekerasan antara lain:
a. kekerasan fisik;
b. kekerasan psikis;
c. kekerasan seksual;
d. penelantaran;
e. eksploitasi; dan/atauf. kekerasan lainnya.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III

ACTS OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN

Article 7

Forms of violence include:

a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.

text:
Pasal 10

Kekerasan seksual sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 huruf (c) disebabkan karena:
a. perbuatan yang berupa pelecehan seksual;
b. pemaksaan hubungan seksual;
c. pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan tidak wajar; dan/atau d. pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan orang lain untuk tujuan komersial  dan atau tujuan tertentu.

translated_text:
Article 10

Sexual violence as referred to in Article 7 letter (c) is caused by:

a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced unnatural sexual intercourse; and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial purposes and or certain purposes.

text:
Pasal 11

Penelantaran sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 huruf d disebabkan  karena:
a. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya kebutuhan anak  secara wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual maupun sosial yang dilakukan  oleh orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggungjawab  atas pengasuhannya;
b. perbuatan mengabaikan dengan sengaja untuk memelihara, merawat, atau mengurus anak sebagaimana mestinya yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggungjawab atas  pengasuhannya;
c. perbuatan yang menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah tangganya,  padahal menurut hukum yang berlaku baginya atau karena persetujuan  atau perjanjian ia wajib memberikan kehidupan, perawatan, atau  pemeliharaan kepada orang tersebut; dand. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara  membatasi dan/atau melarang untuk bekerja yang layak di dalam atau di  luar rumah sehingga korban berada dibawah kendali orang tersebut.

translated_text:
Article 11

Neglect as referred to in Article 7 letter (d) is caused by:

a. acts that result in the unfulfillment of a child's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social carried out by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or take care of a child as appropriate carried out by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and
d. acts that result in economic dependence by limiting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

text:
Pasal 14

1. Upaya pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak dilakukan  secara terpadu oleh Pemerintah Daerah yang dikoordinasikan oleh SKPD yang mempunyai tugas pokok dan fungsi koordinasi dibidang  pemberdayaan perempuan, keluarga berencana dan perlindungan anak.
2. Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan  dengan cara:a. menyusun Program Aksi dan kegiatan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan  Anak dalam Rencana Strategis;
b. membentuk jaringan kerja dalam upaya pencegahan kekerasan; c. melakukan koordinasi, integrasi, dan sinkronisasi pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak.  d. membentuk sistem pencegahan kekerasan;
e. melakukan sosialisasi tentang peraturan perundang-undangan yang  berkaitan dengan hak-hak dan perlindungan perempuan dan anak  terhadap tindak kekerasan;
f. memberikan pendidikan kritis tentang hak-hak perempuan dan anak  kepada masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 14

1. Efforts to prevent violence against women and children are carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the SKPD which has the main tasks and functions of coordination in the field of women's empowerment, family planning and child protection.
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by means of:
a. preparing Action Programs and activities for Women and Children Empowerment in the Strategic Plan;
b. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence;
c. conducting coordination, integration, and synchronization of prevention of violence against women and children.
d. establishing a violence prevention system;
e. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the rights and protection of women and children against acts of violence;
f. providing critical education about the rights of women and children to the community.

text:
Pasal 16

Penyelenggaraan pelayanan terhadap korban dilaksanakan dengan prinsip:
a. cepat;
b. aman dan nyaman;
c. rasa empati;
d. non diskriminasi;
e. mudah dijangkau;
f. tidak dikenakan biaya; dang. dijamin kerahasiaannya.

translated_text:
Article 16

The provision of services to victims is implemented with the principles of:

a. fast;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. sense of empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible;
f. not charged; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.

text:
Pasal 17

Bentuk pelayanan terhadap korban meliputi:
a. pelayanan pengaduan, konsultasi, dan konseling;
b. pelayanan pendampingan;
c. pelayanan kesehatan;
d. pelayanan pemulihan sosial;
e. pelayanan hukum; danf. pelayanan pemulangan dan penyatuan kembali dalam masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 17

Forms of services to victims include:

a. complaint, consultation, and counseling services;
b. assistance services;
c. health services;
d. social recovery services;
e. legal services; and
f. return and reintegration services into society.

text:
Pasal 19

Pelayanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 17 huruf b  meliputi:
a. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan dan pemulihan  kesehatan;
b. mendampingi korban selama proses medicolegal;
c. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan di Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan pengadilan;
d. memantau kepentingan dan hak-hak korban dalam proses pemeriksaan di Kepolisan, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;
e. menjaga privasi dan kerahasiaan korban dari semua pihak yang tidak  berkepentingan, termasuk pemberitaan oleh media massa;
f. melakukan koordinasi dengan pendamping yang lain;dan g. memberikan penanganan yang berkelanjutan hingga tahap pemulihan.

translated_text:
Article 19

Assistance services as referred to in Article 17 letter b include:

a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the medicolegal process;
c. accompanying victims during the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and court;
d. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
e. maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by the mass media;
f. coordinating with other assistants; and
g. providing continuous handling up to the recovery stage.

text:
Pasal 22

Pelayanan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 17 huruf e untuk  membantu korban dalam menjalani proses peradilan dengan cara:
a. memberikan konsultasi hukum yang mencakup informasi mengenai hak hak korban dan proses peradilan;
b. mendampingi korban ditingkat penyidikan, penuntutan, dan pemeriksaan  dalam siding pengadilan dan membantu korban untuk secara lengkap memaparkan kekerasan yang dialaminya;
c. melakukan koordinasi dengan sesama penegak hukum, relawan  pendamping, dan pekerja sosial agar proses peradilan berjalan  sebagaimana mestinya.

translated_text:
Article 22

Legal services as referred to in Article 17 letter e to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process by:

a. providing legal consultation that includes information regarding the rights of victims and the judicial process;
b. accompanying victims at the investigation, prosecution, and examination levels in court hearings and helping victims to fully describe the violence they experienced;
c. coordinating with fellow law enforcers, volunteer assistants, and social workers so that the judicial process runs as it should.

text:
BAB IV

KEWAJIBAN DAN TANGGUNG JAWAB

Pasal 28

Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan  terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan merupakan  tanggungjawab bersama yaitu:
a. Pemerintah Daerah;
b. Pemerintah Desa dan Lembaga Adat Kutei Desa/Kelurahan c. masyarakat;
d. keluarga;
e. orangtua; danf. lembaga terkait baik langsung maupun tidak langsung.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IV

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 28

Obligations and responsibilities in the provision of protection for women and children from acts of violence are the shared responsibility of:

a. Regional Government;
b. Village Government and Kutei Traditional Institutions of Village/Sub-district;
c. community;
d. family;
e. parents; and
f. related institutions both directly and indirectly.

text:
Pasal 29

1. Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab pemerintah daerah sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 28 huruf a, meliputi:a. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan  anak dari tindak kekerasan yang ditetapkan oleh pemerintah; b. menetapkan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
c. membentuk lembaga P2TP2A;
d. melakukan kerjasama dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
e. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan  perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan; f. mengalokasikan anggaran penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan sesuai kemampuan  keuangan daerah;
g. membina dan mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
h. melakukan kerjasama penanganan tindak kekerasan terhadap  perempuan dan anak dengan Daerah lain atau lembaga dan pihak  terkait; dani. melakukan evaluasi atas program dan kegiatan perlindungan  perempuan dan anak terhadap tindak kekerasan.
2. SKPD yang mempunyai tugas pokok dan fungsi dibidang pemberdayaan  perempuan, keluarga berencana dan perlindungan anak melakukan  koordinasi, sinkronisasi dan evaluasi perlindungan perempuan dan anak  terhadap tindak kekerasan dengan melibatkan pihak-pihak terkait paling  sedikit 6 (enam) bulan sekali.
3. Dalam rangka melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung jawab  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah Daerah menetapkan  program dan kegiatan aksi perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak  dalam 1 (satu) Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagai dasar bagi SKPD terkait dalam melaksanakan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari  tindak kekerasan.
4. Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3), merupakan  bagian Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Menengah Daerah (RPJMD). (5) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (4), diatur dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 29

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 28 letter a, include:
a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence as determined by the Government;
b. stipulating policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. forming the P2TP2A institution;
d. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
f. allocating a budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity;
g. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
h. conducting cooperation in handling acts of violence against women and children with other Regions or related institutions and parties; and
i. conducting evaluation of programs and activities for the protection of women and children against acts of violence.
2. SKPD having main duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment, family planning and child protection shall coordinate, synchronize and evaluate the protection of women and children against acts of violence by involving related parties at least once every 6 (six) months.
3. In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall establish programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in 1 (one) Regional Action Plan as a basis for related SKPD in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
4. The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (3), constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).
5. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (4), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 31

Pemerintahan Desa dalam perlindungan perempuan dan anak terhadap  tindak kekerasan mempunyai peran:
a. turut secara aktif mencegah terjadinya kekerasan fisik, kekerasan  psikis, kekerasan seksual, penelantaran, eksploitasi, dan/atau kekerasan  lainnya terhadap perempuan dan anak;
b. melindungi korban;
c. mengamankan pelaku yang tertangkap tangan dan barang bukti  sebelum diserahkan pada yang berwajib;
d. berdasarkan pada permintaan korban Pemerintah Desa menyerahkan  pelaku pada Kepolisian Republik Indonesia, jika terdapat unsur  pidana;dane. memberikan pertolongan darurat.

translated_text:
Article 31

Village Government in the protection of women and children against acts of violence has the role of:

a. actively participating in preventing the occurrence of physical violence, psychological violence, sexual violence, neglect, exploitation, and/or other violence against women and children;
b. protecting victims;
c. securing perpetrators caught red-handed and evidence before handing them over to the authorities;
d. based on the victim's request, the Village Government shall hand over the perpetrator to the Indonesian National Police, if there are criminal elements; and
e. providing emergency assistance.

text:
Pasal 32

Kutei Desa dan/atau Kutei Kelurahan mempunyai kewajiban dan tanggung  jawab dalam hal sebagai berikut:
a. turut secara aktif mencegah terjadinya kekerasan fisik, kekerasan  psikis, kekerasan seksual, penelantaran, eksploitasi, dan/atau kekerasan  lainnya terhadap perempuan dan anak berdasarkan ketentuan hukum adat;
b. melakukan penyelesaian tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan  anak jika terjadi pelanggaran norma hukum adat;
c. ikut serta melakukan pengawasan penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak yang dilakukan oleh pemerintah maupun lembaga lainnya.

translated_text:
Article 32

Kutei Desa and/or Kutei Kelurahan have obligations and responsibilities in the following matters:

a. actively participating in preventing the occurrence of physical violence, psychological violence, sexual violence, neglect, exploitation, and/or other violence against women and children based on customary law provisions;
b. conducting resolution of acts of violence against women and children if violations of customary law norms occur;
c. participating in supervising the implementation of protection of women and children carried out by the government or other institutions.

text:
Pasal 33

Masyarakat dan keluarga mempunyai kewajiban dan tanggung jawab dalam  hal sebagai berikut:
a. mencegah terjadinya kekerasan fisik, kekerasan psikis, kekerasan  seksual, penelantaran, eksploitasi, dan/atau kekerasan lainnya terhadap perempuan dan anak;
b. melaporkan bila terjadi kekerasan;
c. melindungi korban;
d. memberikan pengaman bagi pelaku yang tertangkap tangan; dan e. memberikan pertolongan darurat.  f. ikut serta melakukan pengawasan penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak yang dilakukan oleh pemerintah maupun lembaga lainnya.

translated_text:
Article 33

The community and family have obligations and responsibilities in the following matters:

a. preventing the occurrence of physical violence, psychological violence, sexual violence, neglect, exploitation, and/or other violence against women and children;
b. reporting if violence occurs;
c. protecting victims;
d. providing security for perpetrators caught red-handed; and
e. providing emergency assistance.
f. participating in supervising the implementation of protection of women and children carried out by the government or other institutions.

text:
Pasal 39

1. Struktur organisasi P2TP2A yang dibentuk oleh Pemerintah Daerah  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 19 ayat (1) terdiri dari: a. ketua umum atau sebutan lain yang setingkat;
b. sekretaris;
c. bendahara; dand. ketua pelaksana yang membawahi bidang-bidang.
2. Bidang-Bidang sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) huruf d, sekurang kurangnya meliputi:a. bidang layanan pengaduan;
b. bidang layanan kesehatan;
c. bidang layanan pemulihan sosial;
d. bidang pemulangan dan penyatuan kembali dalam masyarakat;dan  e. bidang layanan advokasi dan bantuan hukum.
3. Struktur organisasi P2TP2A sebagaimana dimaksud ayat (1) ditetapkan  oleh Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 39

1. The organizational structure of P2TP2A formed by the Regional Government as referred to in Article 19 paragraph (1) consists of:
a. general chairperson or other equivalent designation;
b. secretary;
c. treasurer; and
d. executive chairperson overseeing fields.
2. The Fields as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d, at minimum include:
a. complaints service field;
b. health service field;
c. social recovery service field;
d. repatriation and reintegration into society field; and
e. advocacy and legal aid service field.
3. The organizational structure of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be established by the Regent.

text:
Pasal 40

Bidang layanan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 39 ayat (2) huruf a memiliki tugas:
a. melakukan wawancara dan observasi keadaan korban;
b. membuat rekomendasi layanan lanjutan;
c. melakukan koordinasi dan rujukan kelayanan lanjutan dengan pihak terkait;dand. melakukan administrasi proses pengaduan.

translated_text:
Article 40

The complaints service field as referred to in Article 39 paragraph (2) letter a has the duties of:

a. conducting interviews and observation of the victim's condition;
b. making recommendations for follow-up services;
c. conducting coordination and referral of follow-up services with related parties; and
d. conducting administration of the complaint process.

text:
Pasal 41

Bidang layanan kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 39 ayat (2) huruf b memiliki tugas:
a. melakukan pemeriksaan, pengobatan, dan perawatan lanjutan terhadap  korban;
b. melakukan koordinasi pelaksanaan pemulihan kesehatan dan  medicolegal;
c. melakukan pemeriksaan medicolegal meliputi pengumpulan barang bukti  pada korban dan pembuatan visum et repertum;
d. melakukan pemeriksaan penunjang dan laboratorium terhadap barang  bukti;
e. melakukan konsultasi kepada dokter ahli atau melakukan rujukan; dan  f. membuat laporan kasus.

translated_text:
Article 41

The health service field as referred to in Article 39 paragraph (2) letter b has the duties of:

a. conducting examination, treatment, and follow-up care of victims;
b. conducting coordination of health recovery implementation and medicolegal;
c. conducting medicolegal examination including collection of evidence from victims and preparation of visum et repertum;
d. conducting supporting examinations and laboratory tests on evidence;
e. conducting consultation with specialist doctors or making referrals; and
f. making case reports.
